  "frame_trim": "entity-level canvas: all frames of one entity share frame_size and a fixed content offset (union of every frame's ink bbox, cell-relative), then each animation is shifted vertically so its feet line lands on the entity feet line (`baseline.feet_y`, taken from the walk animation). `y_shift` = px the animation was moved down (+ = content moved down); it is a per-frame list for `dead`, whose lying pose rests on the ground line. `cell_offset`/`cell_size` locate the canvas origin inside the source cell.",
  "notes": [
   "sheets are NOT uniform 5-row grids: characters are laid out row-major, 8 cells/row, frames grouped into animations by the declared frame counts",
   "knight attack1 = horizontal thrust, attack2 = slash (last 8 cells of row 3)",
   "archer arrow.png sits in the cell right after the attack frames",
   "heart_empty.png absent from source art",
   "player/enemies entities carry a `baseline` entry next to the animation entries: skip keys whose value has no `frames`"
  ]
 }
